.Dd September 6, 2026
.Dt LIBCRYPTOCMP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cryptocmp_open ,
.Nm cryptocmp_close ,
.Nm cryptocmp_generate ,
.Nm cryptocmp_generate_key ,
.Nm cryptocmp_digest ,
.Nm cryptocmp_random ,
.Nm cryptocmp_named_create ,
.Nm cryptocmp_named_lease ,
.Nm cryptocmp_named_rotate ,
.Nm cryptocmp_named_delete ,
.Nm cryptocmp_named_stat
.Nd public client for the system crypto broker
.Sh LIBRARY
.Li libcryptocmp
.Pq Fl lcryptocmp
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In cryptocmp.h
.Ft int
.Fn cryptocmp_open "struct cryptocmp_client **client"
.Ft void
.Fn cryptocmp_close "struct cryptocmp_client *client"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptocmp_generate "struct cryptocmp_client *client" "const struct cryptocmp_generate *params" "int *fdp"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptocmp_generate_key "struct cryptocmp_client *client" "const struct cryptocmp_key_generate *params" "uint8_t public_key[32]" "int *fdp"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptocmp_digest "struct cryptocmp_client *client" "uint32_t alg" "uint32_t ttl" "uint32_t flags" "int *fdp"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptocmp_random "struct cryptocmp_client *client" "void *buf" "size_t nbytes"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptocmp_named_create "struct cryptocmp_client *client" "const char *name" "const struct cryptocmp_generate *params" "uint64_t *generationp"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptocmp_named_lease "struct cryptocmp_client *client" "const char *name" "uint32_t rights" "uint32_t ttl" "uint64_t *generationp" "int *fdp"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptocmp_named_rotate "struct cryptocmp_client *client" "const char *name" "uint64_t *generationp"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptocmp_named_delete "struct cryptocmp_client *client" "const char *name" "uint64_t *generationp"
.Ft int
.Fn cryptocmp_named_stat "struct cryptocmp_client *client" "const char *name" "struct cryptocmp_named_info *info"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library is the client for the
.Dv system.Crypto
broker (interface version
.Dv 3.2.0 ) .
The broker mints kernel OpenCrypto session descriptors and produces random
bytes under the caller's serviced-authenticated identity.
Named keys are owned by the session's channel label, which is never supplied on
the wire, so a caller can only ever observe or operate on keys minted under its
own label.
.Pp
.Fn cryptocmp_open
resolves the broker over the
.Xr libservice 3
lookup channel and returns a process-bound client handle in
.Fa client .
.Fn cryptocmp_close
releases it.
.Pp
.Fn cryptocmp_generate
mints an ephemeral symmetric-crypto session from the algorithm profile in
.Fa params
and returns its descriptor in
.Fa fdp .
The
.Vt struct cryptocmp_generate
profile selects the cipher, MAC, key and IV lengths, granted rights, and a
time-to-live; a
.Fa flags
value of
.Dv CRYPTOCMP_GENERATE_F_NIST_APPROVED_ONLY
restricts the selection to NIST-approved algorithms.
Selecting a profile is not a FIPS validation claim.
.Pp
.Fn cryptocmp_generate_key
mints an ephemeral asymmetric key session, returning the public key in the
32-byte
.Fa public_key
buffer and the session descriptor in
.Fa fdp .
.Pp
.Fn cryptocmp_digest
mints an ephemeral unkeyed-hash session for the OpenCrypto plain-hash selector
.Fa alg
(for example
.Dv CRYPTO_SHA2_256 )
with the given
.Fa ttl
and
.Fa flags ,
returning the descriptor in
.Fa fdp .
Because there is no key material, the descriptor is not owner-scoped.
.Pp
.Fn cryptocmp_random
fills
.Fa buf
with
.Fa nbytes
of CSPRNG output.
A single request is bounded by
.Dv CRYPTOCMP_MAX_RANDOM_BYTES .
.Pp
.Fn cryptocmp_named_create
creates a persistent named key
.Fa name
from the profile in
.Fa params ,
storing its initial generation number in
.Fa generationp .
.Fn cryptocmp_named_lease
mints a fresh session descriptor for an existing named key with the requested
.Fa rights
and
.Fa ttl ,
returning the current generation in
.Fa generationp
and the descriptor in
.Fa fdp .
.Fn cryptocmp_named_rotate
rotates the named key's underlying material, advancing and returning its new
generation in
.Fa generationp .
.Fn cryptocmp_named_delete
destroys the named key and returns its final generation in
.Fa generationp .
.Pp
.Fn cryptocmp_named_stat
resolves a named key by
.Pq owner , name
and returns its metadata in
.Fa info
without minting a descriptor or mutating the key: no descriptor is delivered
and the generation is unchanged.
The
.Vt struct cryptocmp_named_info
reports the current
.Va generation ,
the granted rights mask, the cipher and MAC selectors (zero when none), and the
cipher and MAC key lengths.
A key absent under the caller's own label is reported with
.Er ENOENT .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Functions returning
.Vt int
return zero on success and \-1 on failure with
.Va errno
set.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libservice 3 ,
.Xr crypto 4 ,
.Xr localcrypto 8
